<title>AUSTRALIA: Highest/Lowest Australian P-E Ratios - April 10.</title>
<headline>Highest/Lowest Australian P-E Ratios - April 10.</headline>
<dateline>SYDNEY 1996-04-10</dateline>
<text>
<p>Highest and lowest price earnings ratios for Australian companies included in the 320-company All Ordinaries Index based on closing prices on Wednesday. P/E based on rolling 12 months earnings.</p>
<p>Highest 10</p>
<p>Rank Name		     P/E    Close</p>
<p> 1   Mayne Nickless	357.14    7.75</p>
<p> 2   Kidston Gold	  250.00    1.20</p>
<p> 3   Mt Edon Gold	  243.96    2.22</p>
<p> 4   Ranger Minerals     193.78    4.05</p>
<p> 5   Perilya Mines	 193.02    0.83</p>
<p> 6   Equatorial Min	133.33    0.24</p>
<p> 7   St.Barbara Mine     107.04    0.76</p>
<p> 8   Westpac Prop Tr     106.25    1.70</p>
<p> 9   Consol Paper	   85.29    2.90</p>
<p>10   Devex		    73.33    0.33</p>
<p>Lowest 10</p>
<p> 1   Climax Mining	   1.67    0.83</p>
<p> 2   Consol Rutile	   4.37    0.98</p>
<p> 3   Jardine Fm China	4.37    0.65</p>
<p> 4   BTR Plc		   5.37    5.00</p>
<p> 5   Premier Inv	     5.94    1.40</p>
<p> 6   OLS Asia Hldgs	  6.08    0.87</p>
<p> 7   Adel Bton Cement	7.01    1.68</p>
<p> 8   BT Aust Eq Mgmt	 7.13    0.72</p>
<p> 9   Renison Goldflds	7.13    4.86</p>
<p>10   FAI Life Ltd	    7.45    0.74</p>
<p>-- Sydney Newsroom 61-2 373-1800</p>
</text>
